{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift.geom_gives_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift.geom_gives_lift","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L254-L254","doc":"The derived (not fitted) amplitude drives the even-face correction to the physical\n**lift** `κ_phys`, which strictly EXCEEDS `1` — an enhancement provably outside the\nself-adjoint branching route (`A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift.anti_self_adjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift.anti_self_adjoint","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L250-L250","doc":"The geometrically-derived amplitude BREAKS graded self-adjointness: `E_geom ≠ 0`,\ni.e. `C_geom = −(σ B_geom) + E_geom ≠ −(σ B_geom)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift.mk","kind":"ctor","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L246-L246","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.DerivedAmplitudeGivesLift","kind":"class","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L217-L255","doc":"**§3b dependent conjecture — the A=3 lift closes via a DERIVED anti-self-adjoint\namplitude.**\n\n`@conjecture: dependent` (its content depends on the open geometric derivation of the\nanti-self-adjoint amplitude — `conj:qdifference-kernel-prolongation-symbol` / the\n`qou-jqof` wall — supplying `E_geom` as the Yekutieli-Stokes prolongation symbol of\nthe SW connection).\n\nThe claim: a geometrically-derived amplitude `E_geom` (an INPUT from the DM q-cubic,\nindependent of the physical target) simultaneously (i) **breaks** graded\nself-adjointness (`E_geom ≠ 0`, i.e. the derived off-block `C_geom = −(σ B_geom) +\nE_geom` differs from its self-adjoint value `−(σ B_geom)` — the anti-self-adjoint\namplitude the branching leaves free) and (ii) drives the even-face correction to a\nphysical **lift** `κ_phys > 1` (unreachable by the self-adjoint branching Schur\ncomplement, `A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one`).\n\nThe bar involution `σ` is quantified as a genuine ring homomorphism applied to the\nderived off-block magnitude `B_geom`; the self-adjoint reference value is `−(σ\nB_geom)`.\n\n**Why this is content-bearing and NOT a fit.**  In a *fit* `E` is solved from\n`κ_phys` (`amplitude_surjective`, witness `E* = (factor_sa − κ)·A·D·B⁻¹`).  Here\n`E_geom` is a *given* geometric input and the conjunction is a nontrivial *check*\nthat the geometry both breaks self-adjointness AND lands the physics — false for a\ngeneric `E_geom`, and (by `amplitude_nonzero`) the `E_geom ≠ 0` clause is *forced* by\nthe strict lift, tying the two fields together.  **No instance is supplied**:\nderiving `E_geom` from the prolongation symbol IS the open keystone; discharging this\nby *choosing* `E_geom` to hit `κ_phys` would be the forbidden fit and is explicitly\nnot done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_injective","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L192-L207","doc":"**The amplitude realizing a given factor is UNIQUE (sorry-free).**  For fixed\nnonzero background `A, B, D`, `E ↦ factor` is injective.  Together with Part 3 it is\na **bijection**: the A=3 lift is carried by EXACTLY ONE real degree of freedom — the\nanti-self-adjoint amplitude `E`.  There is no residual multiplicity to hide a\nderivation in; deriving that single scalar from the geometry is the whole of the\nopen keystone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L174-L188","doc":"**The anti-self-adjoint amplitude `E` is a FREE parameter (sorry-free).**  For fixed\nnonzero background `A, B, D`, the map `E ↦ evenFaceCorrection A (crossTerm B (Csa + E)\nD)` is **surjective** onto `R`: for ANY target `r` there is an amplitude `E`\nrealizing it — witness `E = (factor_sa − r)·A·D·B⁻¹`.  So the anti-self-adjoint\nroute CAN reach the observed lift `r* ≈ 1.585` (contrast the self-adjoint route,\nscope-(b) excluded), but only by pinning `E` to the target — a FIT, unless `E` is\nderived from an independent geometric datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L158-L170","doc":"**A lift requires `E ≠ 0` — the off-block is anti-self-adjoint (sorry-free).**  The\nlift forces the anti-self-adjoint amplitude `E` itself to be nonzero: the derived\noff-block `C = Csa + E ≠ Csa = −(σ B)`.  This is the precise wall `A3OffBlockDerivation`\nnamed — a lift needs `C ≠ −σ B`.  (The implication `B·D⁻¹·E ≠ 0 ⇒ E ≠ 0` needs no\nside condition: a zero factor kills the product.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lift_forces_nonzero_amplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lift_forces_nonzero_amplitude","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L142-L156","doc":"**A genuine lift forces `B·D⁻¹·E ≠ 0` (sorry-free).**  If the self-adjoint\nbackground factor is `≤ 1` (proved for the branching by\n`A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one`) and the full factor is a lift\n(`> 1`), then the amplitude term `B·D⁻¹·E` is nonzero.  Contrapositive: with `E = 0`\nthe factor is the self-adjoint value `≤ 1` — no lift.  The lift lives ENTIRELY in\nthe anti-self-adjoint amplitude the branching leaves free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.factor_affine_in_amplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.factor_affine_in_amplitude","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L123-L138","doc":"**The even-face factor splits as `factor_sa − (slope)·E` (sorry-free).**  Writing the\noff-block as `C = Csa + E` (`Csa = −(σ B)` the graded-self-adjoint value, `E` the\nanti-self-adjoint amplitude), the even-face correction is affine in `E`:\n\n  `evenFaceCorrection A (crossTerm B (Csa + E) D)`\n    `= evenFaceCorrection A (crossTerm B Csa D) − B·D⁻¹·E / A`.\n\nThe first term is the self-adjoint background (`≤ 1`, `A3OffBlockDerivation`); the\nsecond is the lift the amplitude `E` supplies, linear in `E` with slope `B·D⁻¹/A`.\nThe identity is a pure field manipulation — it holds for ALL `A, B, D` (the physical\nregime has `A, D` invertible even/odd blocks; the split needs no side condition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.evenFaceCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.evenFaceCorrection","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L117-L119","doc":"The multiplicative **even-face correction** `(A − t)/A` the cross-term `t` supplies\nto the bar-even (mass / C1) face. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.crossTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.crossTerm","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.lean#L113-L115","doc":"The Berezinian **cross-term** `t = B·D⁻¹·C` (grade-reversing off-blocks `B, C`\nbridged by the odd-block inverse `D⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}